  "officialAlternative": {
    "url": "https://www.organisatiegids.universiteitleiden.nl/reglementen/geesteswetenschappen/oer/latijns-amerikastudies-ba",
    "inspection": "The official programme regulation index retrieved via web lists the 2026–2027 regulation and earlier editions. No 2027–2028 or 2028–2029 bridge is listed. Guessed later PDF URLs returned access-block HTML in direct retrieval and the 2027–2028 path was inaccessible through web retrieval. These attempts do not establish whether an unpublished rule exists."
  },
  "findings": [
    "The annual BA-LAS PRG footnote explicitly moves the 2026 entrants’ placement to semester one of year two. BA-LAS-2-K contains BLV-S2 only, and the current module gives 30 EC and S2. The two required and three Spanish-track taught courses total 30 EC under the earlier timing. The response for guessed BLV-S1 in the current year is JSON null.",
    "Eight catalogue product queries for four nominal academic years in both languages returned byte-identical 2026–2027 records. In particular 2271 and 2281 did not return the cohort’s years two and three. This is insufficient to assume the earlier taught modules move intact or to confirm the later electives, credit allocation and thesis pathway for the revised cohort.",
    "The existing formal §4.2.1 progression findings remain usable: the first-year diploma is required before study abroad, methods and third-year electives, and the named methods course precedes the thesis seminar and thesis. The known progression rule does not establish revised semester offerings. The public programme guide, archive and targeted indexed searches supplied no cohort-specific course allocation."
  ],
  "unresolved": "Obtain an authoritative course and credit allocation for the September 2026 Spanish-path entrants in years two and three. In particular confirm how the 30 EC of year-two taught courses fit after the cohort’s first-semester study abroad and which later-year requirements carry forward.",
  "retryDisposition": "Second unsuccessful essential-source execution. Preserve the 60 EC partial curriculum and existing review. Operational deferral follows published evidence and CI verification. Separate revisit unused."
}
